From f675d91d4b7931afd0af6c7737635a08c8c476da Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Simone Primarosa <3505087+simonepri@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 16:35:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Keep PC sampling off when the driver denies profiling

With the NVIDIA driver's default NVreg_RestrictProfilingToAdminUsers=1,
only processes with CAP_SYS_ADMIN may use the performance counters PC
sampling needs. CUPTI doesn't say so up front: cuptiPCSamplingEnable and
the configuration calls succeed, and at the first module load or kernel
launch CUPTI fails with CUPTI_ERROR_INSUFFICIENT_PRIVILEGES and calls
cuptiFinalize on itself. That drops parcagpu's subscriber and every
activity kind, so the process reports nothing more: no callbacks, no
kernel activity, no completeBuffer. At exit cuptiEnableCallback on the
dead subscriber fails with CUPTI_ERROR_INVALID_PARAMETER (#59, #60).
A minimal injection that only enables PC sampling and sets a sampling
data buffer, and NVIDIA's pc_sampling_continuous sample, do the same.

PCSampling::isSupported now reads RmProfilingAdminOnly from
/proc/driver/nvidia/params and CapEff from /proc/self/status, and keeps
PC sampling off with a warning when profiling is restricted and the
process lacks CAP_SYS_ADMIN, as the driver's own check does. Kernel
activity and launch probes then keep working, and the agent sees the
process as not PC sampling capable. Without the params file the check
passes, as before.

Fixes #59
